 "y": 284.81249443548205, "width": 64.32222222222218, "height": 22.968760952353477}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "IgE- Immunoglobulin F, COVID-19-coronavirus disease 2019 cause by the novel coronavirus SARS-CoV-2, GI =gastrointestinal", "bbox": {"x": 845.1802917922006, "y": 194.7480153501244, "width": 657.3003849029541, "height": 57.81001107394689}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Table 3 eConsult outcome as determined by specialist", "bbox": {"x": 247.93739638627113, "y": 1934.213367557795, "width": 560.8827055189345, "height": 32.27711798250693}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "glycol (PEG) (Table 2). Other common queries included vaccination safety/efficacy in the setting of various comorbidities, including autoimmune dis-", "bbox": {"x": 151.61666622114478, "y": 1364.34365469641, "width": 661.6, "height": 91.87519276142113}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "ease, history of venous or arterial thrombosis, and immunodeficiency.", "bbox": {"x": 151.19792723518083, "y": 1292.0885167041272, "width": 662.6139381408691, "height": 76.2860640585423}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "An important category of eConsult involved possible reaction to a first dose of the COVID-19 vaccine. Commonly reported concerns included possible IgE-mediated response, delayed skin rashes, and neurologic symptoms such as paresthesia post immunization. This comprised a significant number of Consults, but was likely underrepresented as a whole given rising numbers of first doses rates administered in the latter months of our study [20].", "bbox": {"x": 151.61659553783514, "y": 996.8436485808711, "width": 661.6001402113174, "height": 294.0002278089524}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "The eConsult process did effectively alter the planned clinical path for a significant number of patients studied. 72.1% of Consults reviewed (360/499) were answered by specialist electronically without requirement for external resources or referral to other specialty (lable 3). After completion of consultation, only a small percentage of eConsult responses recommended in-person allergy assessment or another specialist referral. From a PCP perspective (Table 4), although in-person referral was initially considered in 276/499 cases, 220 of the 276 eConsults (79.7%) were ultimately managed without an in-person referral. These rates are higher than those previously documented with other specialties; 38% in a similar study of rheumatology Consults and 66% in a study of hematology eConsults [12-14]. Interestingly, PCPs used the Consult service for 181 patients when they hadn't intended to refer a patient in the first place, and 9 of those Consults lead to formal in-person consultation.", "bbox": {"x": 151.44649323837194, "y": 330.7231404089879, "width": 661.9589760250515, "height": 661.553973197937}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Discussion", "bbox": {"x": 666.1944442070647, "y": 266.4374868112384, "width": 142.42777777777772, "height": 27.56252628564815}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Summary & explanation", "bbox": {"x": 537.5499997823684, "y": 229.68747583228944, "width": 275.6666666666667, "height": 27.56254819035527}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Our study is the first of its kind to describe an eConsult platform as it pertains to clinical questions surrounding", "bbox": {"x": 151.6166664369444, "y": 160.78114922734508, "width": 661.6, "height": 64.31270152330399}}], "ms": 408.598875}